THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Synthea (synthetic patient generator)
  Copyright The MITRE Corporation
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
  https://github.com/synthetichealth/synthea

  The FHIR R4 dataset in data/synthetic/ is deterministically derived from Synthea v4.0.0 output.
  Source identifiers, names, addresses, contact details, and birth dates are removed; Restricted and
  SYNTHETIC security labels, explicit Consent, and Provenance resources are added. Generation
  parameters and source checksums are recorded in data/synthetic/toolchain-lock.json.

  No real patient data is present. Synthea generates statistically realistic but entirely fictional
  patients.

HAPI FHIR JPA Server Starter
  Copyright Smile CDR, Inc. and contributors
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
  https://github.com/hapifhir/hapi-fhir-jpaserver-starter

  Used as a pinned, disposable, loopback-only interoperability lab. It is not deployed, exposed, or
  connected to any production service.

Eclipse Temurin (JRE)
  Copyright Eclipse Foundation and contributors
  Licensed under the Eclipse Public License 2.0 with the GNU Classpath Exception
  https://adoptium.net/

  Used as a pinned container runtime for reproducible Synthea generation only.

Python runtime dependencies
  FastAPI, Pydantic, Uvicorn, PyJWT, and their transitive dependencies. Each is licensed by its own
  authors under its own terms. The complete set, with versions and artifact hashes, is recorded in
  uv.lock and enumerated in evidence/reports/M08-sbom.cdx.json (CycloneDX 1.6).

